set heading(numbering: none)

`big` · magnify · the n-ary version, a large operator with limits.

# Form

`x.big` on a symbol, `(a + b).big` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | The n-ary version, a large operator with limits. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A smaller or larger copy of the base. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

no LaTeX command.

